WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.116
[PHOENIX] The murder at
the French bistro Très Bien

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.408
has served up a full
course of mystery.

00:00:05.491 --> 00:00:07.491
The strange bottle
found in the kitchen,

00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:09.408
chef Armstrong's massive debt,

00:00:09.491 --> 00:00:11.283
the computer virus
that the victim wrote

00:00:11.366 --> 00:00:13.616
worth millions on
the black market,

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.991
and the shadow of the
Cadaverini Crime Family

00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:17.866
looming over it all.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.116
But I was able to figure
out who my imposter was.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.991
A dangerous loan shark.

00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:24.866
There's only one
thing on my menu:

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.616
Justice for Maggey Byrde!

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.325
Her trial heats back up today!

00:02:02.866 --> 00:02:04.325
Good morning, Mister Wright!

00:02:04.408 --> 00:02:05.991
Well, you seem in high spirits!

00:02:06.075 --> 00:02:09.075
Dunno 'bout high spirits.
More like high-strung!

00:02:09.158 --> 00:02:10.575
Now simmer down!

00:02:10.658 --> 00:02:12.075
It's the cops!

00:02:12.158 --> 00:02:13.491
[grunts]

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:16.408
And that's my cue to exit!

00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:17.741
[PHOENIX]
Uh...

00:02:17.825 --> 00:02:20.700
Uh. Maggey, I--

00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:22.783
[GUMSHOE groans]

00:02:22.866 --> 00:02:26.741
By the way, pal, the lab
results on this came in.

00:02:28.158 --> 00:02:30.533
[gasps] They said it was
full of poison, didn't they?

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.116
Sorry, but sadly for us,

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.158
it's a harmless bottle
of ear medicine.

00:02:34.241 --> 00:02:35.325
You don't say.

00:02:35.408 --> 00:02:37.450
The victim had a
ruptured eardrum.

00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:39.908
This has to be what he was
prescribed to treat it.

00:02:39.991 --> 00:02:41.783
[PHOENIX]
What was Glen Elg's ear medicine

00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:43.366
doing in the kitchen?

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.658
We were able to find some
unknown fingerprints

00:02:45.741 --> 00:02:47.158
on the bottle.

00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:49.116
They're trying to turn up a
match down at the precinct,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.908
so I'd better run back
to check on that.

00:02:50.991 --> 00:02:51.616
See ya!

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.616
[GUMSHOE screams]

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:53.825
What's wrong?

00:02:53.908 --> 00:02:55.408
[GUMSHOE]
Almost forgot.

00:02:55.491 --> 00:02:58.283
How did that lunch I made
for her yesterday turn out?

00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:00.283
Uh... Well, it was, uh...

00:03:00.366 --> 00:03:01.658
It was delicious!

00:03:01.741 --> 00:03:04.075
That's what she said?
Best news I've heard today!

00:03:04.158 --> 00:03:06.325
She may not have used
those words exactly.

00:03:06.408 --> 00:03:09.158
[MAGGEY] Well, no, I can't
really eat this crap.

00:03:09.241 --> 00:03:11.158
Why don't you take them, Maya?

00:03:11.241 --> 00:03:13.491
[MAYA]
Uhh...

00:03:13.575 --> 00:03:14.825
[GUMSHOE]
Great!

00:03:14.908 --> 00:03:17.366
'Cause I whipped up a
jumbo-sized helping today!

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.783
Oh, yeah!

00:03:18.866 --> 00:03:20.825
She can celebrate her freedom!

00:03:20.908 --> 00:03:22.033
[GUMSHOE yells]

00:03:22.116 --> 00:03:23.908
[PHOENIX] Anyway, I know
the Tiger is the key

00:03:23.991 --> 00:03:25.283
to this whole case.

00:03:25.366 --> 00:03:28.408
I have to find a way
to get him to testify.

00:03:32.616 --> 00:03:34.533
This court is hereby
back in session

00:03:34.616 --> 00:03:36.325
for the trial of
Miss Maggey Byrde.

00:03:36.408 --> 00:03:38.700
Let me remind you that
yesterday we were presented

00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:41.450
with the testimony of
Mister Victor Kudo.

00:03:41.533 --> 00:03:43.158
He claimed to have
witnessed the defendant

00:03:43.241 --> 00:03:45.741
pouring a mysterious powder
in the victim's coffee

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.616
right before he died.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.491
However, this
testimony was plagued

00:03:49.575 --> 00:03:52.158
by some rather troubling
inconsistencies.

00:03:52.241 --> 00:03:54.658
Mister Kudo had stated
that he'd seen the victim

00:03:54.741 --> 00:03:57.825
pick up his coffee
using his left hand.

00:03:57.908 --> 00:04:00.575
But upon examining the mark
on the rim of the cup,

00:04:00.658 --> 00:04:02.783
it clearly shows that he
drank his jitter juice

00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:04.200
with his right hand.

00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:06.366
There was another
questionable point.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.241
He said Elg was
listening to the radio

00:04:08.325 --> 00:04:11.575
with an earphone
in his left ear.

00:04:11.658 --> 00:04:14.033
But Mister Elg's left
eardrum was ruptured,

00:04:14.116 --> 00:04:16.991
so it would've been painful to
be listening through that one.

00:04:17.075 --> 00:04:19.116
Seems like we've got
ourselves a steaming cup

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.450
of contradictions to digest.

00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:23.325
Cheers.

00:04:23.408 --> 00:04:24.825
[JUDGE]
Very well.

00:04:24.908 --> 00:04:27.950
Let us call upon today's first
witness to take the stand.

00:04:29.825 --> 00:04:32.491
[ARMSTRONG]
Bonjour!

00:04:32.575 --> 00:04:35.450
Jean Armstrong à votre service!

00:04:35.533 --> 00:04:37.783
Génie culinaire!

00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:39.575
Muchas gracias, Señor Chef.

00:04:39.658 --> 00:04:42.658
You were in the kitchen day of
the incident, is that correct?

00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:44.575
[ARMSTRONG]
Oh-la-la!

00:04:44.658 --> 00:04:48.116
Well, monsieur. Aren't you
a yummy little bon-bon?!

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.283
Oh-la-la! C'est magnifique!

00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:53.200
Not my cup of joe.

00:04:53.283 --> 00:04:54.450
Ahem!

00:04:54.533 --> 00:04:57.491
Please remember, you're
here to give testimony.

00:04:57.575 --> 00:04:59.241
Now then, if you would,

00:04:59.325 --> 00:05:01.491
tell the court what happened
that day at Très Bien

00:05:01.575 --> 00:05:02.866
to the best of your ability.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:03.616
Truthfully.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.283
Oui, but of course.

00:05:05.366 --> 00:05:08.408
On z'at afternoon, Monsieur
Elg was at my bistro.

00:05:08.491 --> 00:05:10.658
'E came inside alone.

00:05:10.741 --> 00:05:13.033
Pépé Kudo arrived
not long after 'im.

00:05:13.116 --> 00:05:14.825
When 'e got word 'e
won le grand prix,

00:05:14.908 --> 00:05:18.116
Monsieur Elg became
very aroused, indeed.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.075
Five minutes after
'is 'appy ejaculation,

00:05:20.158 --> 00:05:21.908
a 'orrible scene unfolded.

00:05:21.991 --> 00:05:23.325
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:05:23.408 --> 00:05:25.408
You're cooking up some
falsehoods, aren't you, chef?

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.991
Nani?

00:05:27.075 --> 00:05:29.450
The victim was listening to a
certain radio program that day.

00:05:29.533 --> 00:05:31.408
A show called
"Millionaire Radio."

00:05:31.491 --> 00:05:34.783
It runs every Wednesday
from 1:30 to 1:40 PM.

00:05:34.866 --> 00:05:36.200
And why do you bring 'zis up?

00:05:36.283 --> 00:05:38.033
Well, as Mister Kudo told us.

00:05:38.116 --> 00:05:39.200
[KUDO]
Gotta say,

00:05:39.283 --> 00:05:41.491
that definitely ruined
my javaccino time.

00:05:41.575 --> 00:05:43.075
[MIA]
Your javaccino time?

00:05:43.158 --> 00:05:45.825
[KUDO] My daily routine is to
enjoy a nice cup of javaccino

00:05:45.908 --> 00:05:48.075
at 2 PM sharp every day.

00:05:48.158 --> 00:05:50.950
[PHOENIX]
He said it was 2 PM.

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:53.325
If the incident occurred five
minutes after the victim

00:05:53.408 --> 00:05:54.950
found out he'd won the lottery,

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:57.658
then Mister Kudo could
not have witnessed it.

00:05:57.741 --> 00:05:59.616
Because he wouldn't have
even been in the restaurant

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.658
at that time of day!

00:06:01.741 --> 00:06:04.075
[ARMSTRONG]
Non!

00:06:04.158 --> 00:06:06.116
[PHOENIX]
The earphone in his damaged ear.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.033
The radio program that
should've been long over.

00:06:09.116 --> 00:06:10.575
We can clear up
these contradictions

00:06:10.658 --> 00:06:11.908
with a simple answer!

00:06:11.991 --> 00:06:13.908
The murder Mister Kudo
witnessed on that day

00:06:13.991 --> 00:06:15.950
was nothing more than
an elaborate fake!

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:18.866
You think it was staged? How so?

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.616
[CROWD whispering]

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.700
Are you implying that
the witness was correct

00:06:22.783 --> 00:06:25.408
when he testified the
earphone was in the left ear?

00:06:25.491 --> 00:06:27.950
The reenactment was
elaborate, not perfect.

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:29.950
Perhaps because the murderer
simply didn't know

00:06:30.033 --> 00:06:31.616
about the victim's
ruptured eardrum.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.533
[GODOT]
Objection!

00:06:33.616 --> 00:06:36.158
If you're truly serious
about that theory,

00:06:36.241 --> 00:06:37.783
let me ask you somethin'.

00:06:37.866 --> 00:06:40.366
When the fake was putting on
the act for the old man,

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.158
tell me, where was
the real Glen Elg?

00:06:42.241 --> 00:06:44.325
By then, he'd already
been poisoned.

00:06:44.408 --> 00:06:46.616
[GODOT] But that would've
left behind a corpse.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.366
Surely they wouldn't
have left his body

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.366
lying around the bistro.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.283
It stands to reason the killer
must've hidden it nearby.

00:06:53.366 --> 00:06:55.033
Maybe in Très Bien's kitchen.

00:06:55.116 --> 00:06:56.491
Mon dieu!

00:06:56.575 --> 00:06:58.950
[PHOENIX] Mister Armstrong,
do you recognize this?

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:00.575
I 'ave never seen zat before!

00:07:00.658 --> 00:07:03.075
All ze bottles I use
are cute and delicate!

00:07:03.158 --> 00:07:05.741
This particular one was found
inside Très Bien's kitchen.

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:08.116
Why would that 'orribly
plain zing be zere?

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.825
What a pertinent question.

00:07:09.908 --> 00:07:12.408
Analysis shows this bottle
contains the ear medicine

00:07:12.491 --> 00:07:13.616
prescribed to the victim.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.616
Non, but 'ow could zat be?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.116
It must've fallen
out of his pocket

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.075
while his body was
being stowed there.

00:07:19.158 --> 00:07:21.491
So, let me ask you this!

00:07:21.575 --> 00:07:22.991
You were back in
Très Bien's kitchen

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.158
when the incident
occurred, were you not?

00:07:25.241 --> 00:07:26.825
Sacre bleu!

00:07:26.908 --> 00:07:28.241
Immediately after the incident,

00:07:28.325 --> 00:07:30.200
you told Victor Kudo
to call the police,

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:31.575
causing him to leave the scene.

00:07:31.658 --> 00:07:33.450
The only witness was
gone for ten minutes,

00:07:33.533 --> 00:07:35.325
which the killer
put to good use.

00:07:35.408 --> 00:07:37.450
In that time, he took the
body back to the table

00:07:37.533 --> 00:07:39.783
and put the bottle of poison in
the pocket of the defendant

00:07:39.866 --> 00:07:42.408
who was still unconscious
on the floor, right?

00:07:42.491 --> 00:07:43.533
[gasps]

00:07:43.616 --> 00:07:45.825
Only one person could've
pulled that off.

00:07:45.908 --> 00:07:47.408
You, Chef Armstrong!

00:07:47.491 --> 00:07:51.200
[ARMSTRONG]
Oh! No!

00:07:51.283 --> 00:07:54.366
[CROWD gasping, murmuring]

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.866
Seems the defense has made
a rather stunning allegation

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.116
that the witness was
the actual perpetrator.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.616
Did you murder Mister Elg?

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.908
No, never, I swear
on everyzing tasty!

00:08:02.991 --> 00:08:05.200
I think scumbags who perjure
themselves in court

00:08:05.283 --> 00:08:06.408
should have their
mouths rinsed out

00:08:06.491 --> 00:08:08.158
with a piping hot pot of coffee.

00:08:08.241 --> 00:08:09.366
No cream or sugar.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.366
[ARMSTRONG gasps]

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.033
Je vous demande
pardon, monsieur!

00:08:12.116 --> 00:08:14.450
Please, you must 'ear me out!

00:08:14.533 --> 00:08:15.950
[JUDGE]
Mhm.

00:08:16.033 --> 00:08:19.325
Tell your story. Remember,
perjury is a serious offense.

00:08:19.408 --> 00:08:21.408
[ARMSTRONG]
Oui. I understand.

00:08:21.491 --> 00:08:24.991
It is true zat I 'id zat man's
lifeless body inside ze kitchen.

00:08:25.075 --> 00:08:28.908
But I 'ad no choice.
Un homme forced me to do it.

00:08:28.991 --> 00:08:30.908
And then you waited
around for ol' bird brain

00:08:30.991 --> 00:08:32.741
to show up like he usually did

00:08:32.825 --> 00:08:34.991
so he could see
the re-enactment.

00:08:35.075 --> 00:08:37.241
But I swear to you I 'ave
never killed anybody

00:08:37.325 --> 00:08:38.491
in my entire life!

00:08:38.575 --> 00:08:40.533
I am not 'zat kind of person!

00:08:40.616 --> 00:08:43.908
Someone forced you into it?
Who was this mystery man?

00:08:43.991 --> 00:08:45.616
My lips, zay must remain sealed,

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:48.408
or else I myself will be
thrown into ze broiler.

00:08:48.491 --> 00:08:49.908
Chef Armstrong. Look.

00:08:49.991 --> 00:08:51.991
We know there's a man
with leverage over you.

00:08:52.075 --> 00:08:54.283
The holder of this loan.

00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:55.700
[gasps]

00:08:55.783 --> 00:08:57.950
You're 500 thousand in the
hole with this loan shark.

00:08:58.033 --> 00:09:00.866
That's why you have no choice
but to do whatever he asks.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:01.700
Right, sir?

00:09:01.783 --> 00:09:03.325
Let ze accusations fly,

00:09:03.408 --> 00:09:05.908
I cannot confirm or deny
zees zings you are saying.

00:09:05.991 --> 00:09:08.366
You are in a very
dangerous situation, sir.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.200
You claim someone
forced you into this,

00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:11.825
so tell us who it was.

00:09:11.908 --> 00:09:14.075
The firm Tender Lender
holds this loan.

00:09:14.158 --> 00:09:14.866
Mon dieu!

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.866
Run by the Big City Tiger.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.033
He made you do it!

00:09:19.116 --> 00:09:20.283
I figured this would happen,

00:09:20.366 --> 00:09:22.991
so I called this wild
tiger in to testify.

00:09:23.075 --> 00:09:24.450
He's here right now.

00:09:24.533 --> 00:09:25.741
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.366
[MAYA screams]

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:29.283
[PHOENIX]
What the--?

00:09:29.366 --> 00:09:33.741
[TIGRE]
You want me?

00:09:36.783 --> 00:09:38.491
[PHOENIX]
This is my big chance!

00:09:38.575 --> 00:09:42.908
So, uh, your name is Mister
Big Tiger, is that correct?

00:09:42.991 --> 00:09:45.533
That's what they
call me! Yeah!

00:09:45.616 --> 00:09:46.700
[grunting]

00:09:46.783 --> 00:09:49.325
[MAYA screams]

00:09:49.408 --> 00:09:50.533
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:09:50.616 --> 00:09:51.741
Who the hell's got the stones

00:09:51.825 --> 00:09:54.158
to call the great Furio
Tigre to this dump?

00:09:54.241 --> 00:09:55.783
Was it you, red eye?

00:09:55.866 --> 00:09:57.616
You know that you don't
have to yell like that.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.741
Yeah?

00:09:58.825 --> 00:10:00.658
But we should expect
a tiger to growl.

00:10:00.741 --> 00:10:03.533
Especially when he's been
trapped in a legal cage.

00:10:05.658 --> 00:10:07.325
Let's start with
the basics, shall we?

00:10:07.408 --> 00:10:09.866
Tell us everything you know
about the incident in question.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:12.158
Ha! I don't know
nuttin', cyclops!

00:10:12.241 --> 00:10:13.533
I'll ask you this.

00:10:13.616 --> 00:10:15.241
Were you a spectator
at Maggey Byrde's

00:10:15.325 --> 00:10:16.783
murder trial a month ago?

00:10:16.866 --> 00:10:19.950
My time's too valuable to waste
it in some courtroom, boul.

00:10:20.033 --> 00:10:21.158
Listen up, smart guy,

00:10:21.241 --> 00:10:23.783
I'll bill ya 50K for
every dumbass question.

00:10:23.866 --> 00:10:26.491
And my interest rate
is a real killer.

00:10:26.575 --> 00:10:28.325
Hey, Nick. You got this!

00:10:28.408 --> 00:10:29.825
Are you hiding?

00:10:29.908 --> 00:10:32.283
So tell us, Mister Tigre,
on the day of the murder,

00:10:32.366 --> 00:10:33.658
you had made plans to meet up

00:10:33.741 --> 00:10:36.033
with Glen Elg at Très Bien
bistro, is that correct?

00:10:36.116 --> 00:10:37.158
What?

00:10:37.241 --> 00:10:38.283
I don't know nuttin'
about none of that

00:10:38.366 --> 00:10:40.450
or what the hell a
tray bee'in even is!

00:10:40.533 --> 00:10:41.575
You're lying to me.

00:10:41.658 --> 00:10:43.033
Nuh-uh!

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.450
[PHOENIX]
Then can you explain this note?

00:10:46.533 --> 00:10:49.283
What the--? Where'd you
get dat from, huh?

00:10:49.366 --> 00:10:53.283
Take these. They may help you.

00:10:53.366 --> 00:10:57.616
Don Tigre. Watch your back.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.450
Viola's medical records.

00:10:59.533 --> 00:11:01.908
[MAYA]
Why did she give those to us?

00:11:01.991 --> 00:11:04.241
"Watch your back," huh?

00:11:04.325 --> 00:11:07.116
Maybe... Check the back?

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.408
[PHOENIX]
Hm.

00:11:08.491 --> 00:11:09.325
[MAYA gasps]

00:11:09.408 --> 00:11:11.075
There it is.

00:11:11.158 --> 00:11:13.408
[PHOENIX]
This note, in your handwriting,

00:11:13.491 --> 00:11:15.325
is decisive proof that
you were planning

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:17.200
to meet the victim
at the crime scene

00:11:17.283 --> 00:11:19.075
the very day he was murdered!

00:11:19.158 --> 00:11:21.616
[yells]

00:11:22.908 --> 00:11:25.616
This calls for another
steaming cup of liquid gold.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.616
[growls]

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.075
That stupid broad.

00:11:29.158 --> 00:11:30.450
Heh!

00:11:30.533 --> 00:11:32.325
What does it matter if I
made plans to meet dat kid?

00:11:32.408 --> 00:11:33.658
Note doesn't say "kill 'em."

00:11:33.741 --> 00:11:36.325
Have you already forgotten
the old man's testimony?

00:11:36.408 --> 00:11:38.825
He stated that the victim
was all alone at his table.

00:11:38.908 --> 00:11:41.700
Have you forgotten about
the defendant's testimony?

00:11:41.783 --> 00:11:43.325
She told the court, under oath,

00:11:43.408 --> 00:11:46.075
there was another man
sitting there that day.

00:11:46.158 --> 00:11:49.033
So that must mean only one
of them is telling the truth.

00:11:49.116 --> 00:11:50.450
You know which one
that would be?

00:11:50.533 --> 00:11:52.075
Well they're both
true, actually.

00:11:52.158 --> 00:11:53.241
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:11:53.325 --> 00:11:55.450
[PHOENIX]
The incident the defendant saw,

00:11:55.533 --> 00:11:57.783
and the incident Mister
Kudo witnessed,

00:11:57.866 --> 00:12:00.366
were two completely different
events altogether.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:01.950
And your theory is
the second one

00:12:02.033 --> 00:12:04.783
was just a little performance
so they could frame the lady?

00:12:04.866 --> 00:12:05.991
Now that's a hot take.

00:12:06.075 --> 00:12:07.116
Yes.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.116
The "victim" Kudo
saw was an imposter

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.450
who was pretending to
be Glen Elg for the show.

00:12:11.533 --> 00:12:13.700
But I know who that phony was.

00:12:13.783 --> 00:12:15.283
And he's right over there.

00:12:15.366 --> 00:12:17.241
Furio Tigre!

00:12:17.325 --> 00:12:20.908
[TIGRE]
Damn you!

00:12:20.991 --> 00:12:21.950
[screams]

00:12:22.033 --> 00:12:22.991
[MAYA screams]

00:12:23.075 --> 00:12:23.950
[BOTH yelp]

00:12:24.033 --> 00:12:25.116
Calm yourself!

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.908
Or I'll have you thrown
out for contempt!

00:12:26.991 --> 00:12:28.533
You'd better stop
with all the banging

00:12:28.616 --> 00:12:30.158
before you get
thrown out with him!

00:12:30.241 --> 00:12:31.658
[JUDGE gasps]

00:12:31.741 --> 00:12:33.616
[PHOENIX] The defendant fell
to the floor unconscious

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.825
immediately after the incident.

00:12:35.908 --> 00:12:37.700
As she lay there,
somebody got the idea

00:12:37.783 --> 00:12:39.991
to try and frame her
for Glen Elg's murder!

00:12:40.075 --> 00:12:41.783
That was when our
feline friend over here

00:12:41.866 --> 00:12:44.033
pretended to be
the victim, right?

00:12:44.116 --> 00:12:46.200
But somebody had to play
the role of the waitress

00:12:46.283 --> 00:12:48.450
serving up his final
cup of the good stuff.

00:12:48.533 --> 00:12:50.200
Viola Cadaverini.

00:12:50.283 --> 00:12:52.908
Who happens to be a
Tender Lender employee.

00:12:52.991 --> 00:12:54.116
[TIGRE growls]

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.575
[TIGRE] Youse makin'
a big mistake wit' her.

00:12:56.658 --> 00:12:59.741
Both she and the Tiger set up
the fake murder together!

00:12:59.825 --> 00:13:01.408
[GODOT]
Objection!

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:06.366
Shouldn't jump to
conclusions, you know?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.116
It's not a good
look for anybody.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.866
What the heck are
you talking about?

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.366
[GODOT] You're overlooking
a critical detail.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.408
There's simply no reason
for the ol' tiger man

00:13:14.491 --> 00:13:15.825
to poison the victim.

00:13:15.908 --> 00:13:16.658
[BOTH]
Uh?

00:13:16.741 --> 00:13:17.950
[grunts]

00:13:18.033 --> 00:13:19.408
It wouldn't make any
sense for me to kill 'em.

00:13:19.491 --> 00:13:22.283
He won 500 grand, but he only
owed me a hundred thou.

00:13:22.366 --> 00:13:24.158
So that means he could pay
back what he borrowed

00:13:24.241 --> 00:13:27.283
and I wouldn't have to do the
wet work and grease nobody.

00:13:27.366 --> 00:13:28.616
[PHOENIX]
But the fact is,

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.325
a hundred thousand wasn't
nearly enough, was it?

00:13:30.408 --> 00:13:31.908
The hell you mean?

00:13:31.991 --> 00:13:34.741
About six months ago, you caused
a traffic accident, didn't you?

00:13:34.825 --> 00:13:36.033
Say what?

00:13:36.116 --> 00:13:37.450
[PHOENIX]
The victim was the granddaughter

00:13:37.533 --> 00:13:40.533
of the head of the
Cadaverini crime family.

00:13:40.616 --> 00:13:42.366
They wanted about
a million from you

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.408
to pay for her
extensive surgeries.

00:13:44.491 --> 00:13:47.075
Which are listed on
her medical file!

00:13:47.158 --> 00:13:49.366
If you didn't compensate
them for the expenses,

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:51.200
you'd be the one
getting "greased."

00:13:51.283 --> 00:13:52.616
So you had to do
whatever it took

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.783
to get your hands on the money.

00:13:54.866 --> 00:13:57.450
Even if he killed Elg and
took his lottery ticket,

00:13:57.533 --> 00:13:59.533
that's half the money
he owed the Cadeverinis.

00:13:59.616 --> 00:14:01.366
He'd still be deep in the
hole for the rest of it.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.366
But it wasn't the
money he was after.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.908
Oh, yeah?

00:14:05.991 --> 00:14:07.491
[PHOENIX]
This is MC Bomber.

00:14:07.575 --> 00:14:10.616
An especially potent computer
virus the victim had written.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.241
Why do youse have dat?

00:14:12.325 --> 00:14:15.908
Glen Elg had a reputation
as a skilled programmer.

00:14:15.991 --> 00:14:18.783
That skill was the collateral
on his loan from you.

00:14:18.866 --> 00:14:21.241
A virus such as this one
could net you millions

00:14:21.325 --> 00:14:22.366
on the black market.

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:24.783
Wow. Millions, you say?

00:14:24.866 --> 00:14:26.283
If you got your
hands on that disc,

00:14:26.366 --> 00:14:28.158
you could pay off
the Cadaverinis.

00:14:28.241 --> 00:14:30.200
That's what you thought, right?

00:14:30.283 --> 00:14:34.158
And so, on that day, when he
won that 500 thousand lottery,

00:14:34.241 --> 00:14:36.741
which meant he wouldn't
have to give you the CD,

00:14:36.825 --> 00:14:39.450
you decided to go
with another plan.

00:14:42.158 --> 00:14:45.575
[PHOENIX] To murder Glen Elg
and steal the virus anyway.

00:14:45.658 --> 00:14:47.325
And then you made
a last-ditch effort

00:14:47.408 --> 00:14:50.241
to frame the defendant
for the crime!

00:14:50.325 --> 00:14:52.866
But that wasn't enough
to satisfy you.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.283
A month ago,

00:14:54.366 --> 00:14:56.408
you pretended to be me in
a trial in this courtroom.

00:14:56.491 --> 00:14:58.658
Really? He impersonated you?

00:14:58.741 --> 00:15:00.991
He posed as her lawyer
in the first hearing

00:15:01.075 --> 00:15:04.075
and made sure to lead her
into a guilty verdict!

00:15:04.158 --> 00:15:05.325
[growls]

00:15:05.408 --> 00:15:08.325
I have to say, this is
making sense to me.

00:15:08.408 --> 00:15:10.991
There's something
familiar about you.

00:15:11.075 --> 00:15:12.658
I'm sorry about the
mix up, your honor,

00:15:12.741 --> 00:15:15.950
but I would never dream
of doin' anything like that.

00:15:16.033 --> 00:15:18.366
I'd say the defense
just got decaffeinated.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.950
What'll you do?

00:15:21.033 --> 00:15:22.241
You scared me!

00:15:22.325 --> 00:15:23.450
[PHOENIX]
I'm so close,

00:15:23.533 --> 00:15:25.991
but I don't have the
evidence to back it up.

00:15:26.075 --> 00:15:29.283
[GUMSHOE]
It's the cops!

00:15:30.491 --> 00:15:31.575
[MAYA, PHOENIX]
Gumshoe's here!

00:15:31.658 --> 00:15:33.575
[GUMSHOE]
I came to drop some evidence!

00:15:33.658 --> 00:15:35.783
And this is gonna clinch
this whole thing up!

00:15:35.866 --> 00:15:36.741
All in the name of love!

00:15:36.825 --> 00:15:38.033
Are you drunk?

00:15:38.116 --> 00:15:39.575
I wonder what he means.

00:15:39.658 --> 00:15:40.950
[growls]

00:15:41.033 --> 00:15:43.116
Turns out, that bottle we'd
found had Furio Tigre's

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.950
grubby fingerprints all over it.

00:15:45.033 --> 00:15:46.783
Huh?

00:15:46.866 --> 00:15:49.158
[MAYA]
That's it, Nick! We did it!

00:15:49.241 --> 00:15:50.366
What's the matter?

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:53.366
This just isn't the
smoking gun we needed.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:54.950
His prints may be on it,

00:15:55.033 --> 00:15:57.616
but that doesn't serve as
a way to prove my theory.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:00.116
He admitted that he'd met with
the victim that same day,

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.658
so he could've
touched the bottle.

00:16:01.741 --> 00:16:03.408
No, that's awful.

00:16:03.491 --> 00:16:06.116
[PHOENIX] I can't prove
my case with evidence.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.033
How can I get myself
out of this corner?

00:16:09.116 --> 00:16:11.700
Come on, Phoenix!
You gotta use your brain!

00:16:11.783 --> 00:16:13.158
So, what now?

00:16:13.241 --> 00:16:15.658
All right. Looks like
you're screwed, boul.

00:16:15.741 --> 00:16:17.658
Defense, would you care
to explain to the court

00:16:17.741 --> 00:16:20.700
what exactly that bottle
has to do with the murder?

00:16:21.741 --> 00:16:23.241
[PHOENIX]
I've got it!

00:16:24.366 --> 00:16:25.825
I would like to
introduce this item

00:16:25.908 --> 00:16:28.700
as the defense's final
piece of evidence.

00:16:28.783 --> 00:16:30.033
Why the hell should
we give a crap

00:16:30.116 --> 00:16:31.908
about that tiny little bottle?

00:16:31.991 --> 00:16:34.033
Because it contains
the potassium cyanide

00:16:34.116 --> 00:16:36.616
that cut Glen Elg's
life short that day.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:37.325
What?

00:16:37.408 --> 00:16:38.616
Pump your brakes, kid.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.408
In other words, your
fingerprints were found

00:16:40.491 --> 00:16:42.700
all over the murder
weapon itself.

00:16:42.783 --> 00:16:44.866
And there's only one way
that could've happened.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:46.491
I think you're
confused, Bubba.

00:16:46.575 --> 00:16:48.366
[TIGRE laughs]

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.741
You're a real clown.

00:16:49.825 --> 00:16:51.075
You should quit your day job,

00:16:51.158 --> 00:16:53.033
especially when you think
a lame bluff like that

00:16:53.116 --> 00:16:55.200
is gonna take down Don Tigre!

00:16:55.283 --> 00:16:56.575
I don't see what's funny.

00:16:56.658 --> 00:16:58.158
The bottle with
the cyanide in it

00:16:58.241 --> 00:17:00.325
wasn't some cheap,
plastic piece of garbage

00:17:00.408 --> 00:17:03.283
it was a nice brown one,
made outta glass.

00:17:07.033 --> 00:17:09.825
[PHOENIX]
He stepped right in it.

00:17:09.908 --> 00:17:11.950
So that's the game
you're playin'. Huh.

00:17:12.033 --> 00:17:13.158
What's the deal?

00:17:13.241 --> 00:17:15.408
Why did everybody
get all quiet-like?

00:17:15.491 --> 00:17:18.533
You described the cyanide
bottle in detail, Tigre.

00:17:18.616 --> 00:17:20.491
Just like this, right?

00:17:20.575 --> 00:17:21.741
Yeah, that's it!

00:17:21.825 --> 00:17:23.116
But youse ain't gonna
find none of my prints

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.408
anywhere on that thing!

00:17:24.491 --> 00:17:26.491
Don't let this clown
pull a fast one on ya!

00:17:26.575 --> 00:17:28.908
Tell 'em they got nothin'
on me, coffee boy!

00:17:28.991 --> 00:17:31.825
I'm guessing you still don't
realize what you just said.

00:17:31.908 --> 00:17:33.783
Rewind your brain a sec
and think about it.

00:17:33.866 --> 00:17:36.033
What I said? Which part of it?

00:17:36.116 --> 00:17:37.825
[PHOENIX] Today was the first
time you'd been summoned

00:17:37.908 --> 00:17:40.075
to the court regarding
Miss Byrde's case.

00:17:40.158 --> 00:17:41.783
If you had nothing to
do with the murder,

00:17:41.866 --> 00:17:44.741
you'd have no way to know
any of the finer details.

00:17:44.825 --> 00:17:47.658
Like what kind of bottle the
poison was in, for example.

00:17:47.741 --> 00:17:49.116
Yeah? Well, I--

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:50.991
[PHOENIX]
You just described it to a tee.

00:17:51.075 --> 00:17:53.991
Then went on to identify it in
front of everyone gathered here.

00:17:54.075 --> 00:17:56.408
Yeah, so what?
I just seen it before.

00:17:56.491 --> 00:17:58.533
They showed it at the
chick's trial last month.

00:17:58.616 --> 00:18:00.450
It is true that the
bottle in question

00:18:00.533 --> 00:18:01.700
was presented as evidence

00:18:01.783 --> 00:18:04.408
in Miss Byrde's first
hearing a month ago.

00:18:04.491 --> 00:18:07.241
However, you stated earlier that
you didn't attend that trial,

00:18:07.325 --> 00:18:10.241
nor knew anything
about the case itself.

00:18:10.325 --> 00:18:11.616
[TIGRE]
I did see it then!

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:13.075
I was right over there.

00:18:13.158 --> 00:18:15.158
Where youse was standin',
playing the defense lawyer.

00:18:15.241 --> 00:18:16.575
And that brown bottle
was brought out

00:18:16.658 --> 00:18:17.741
in front of everyone.

00:18:17.825 --> 00:18:19.325
He was the guy!

00:18:19.408 --> 00:18:21.700
So what you're actually
admitting to, Tiger,

00:18:21.783 --> 00:18:23.366
is that you impersonated
Mister Trite

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.950
in the previous murder trial?

00:18:25.033 --> 00:18:26.241
Uh, that's right!

00:18:26.325 --> 00:18:27.783
I didn't kill the guy,

00:18:27.866 --> 00:18:30.075
I just saw the poison bottle
during dat dog and pony show!

00:18:30.158 --> 00:18:31.741
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:18:34.366 --> 00:18:36.575
[yells]

00:18:36.658 --> 00:18:39.825
Then explain to the court
why you would even do that!

00:18:39.908 --> 00:18:41.366
Why would you go to
all that trouble

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.366
to pretend to be someone's
lawyer in a trial

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:44.700
that had nothing to do with you?

00:18:44.783 --> 00:18:47.325
Look, I, uh.

00:18:47.408 --> 00:18:49.950
[PHOENIX] There's only
one plausible reason.

00:18:50.033 --> 00:18:53.866
You were trying to cover up
a murder you committed!

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.325
I have to appreciate the
irony that a fraud like you

00:18:56.408 --> 00:18:58.075
was brought down by a bluff.

00:18:58.158 --> 00:18:59.950
There's a kind of
"poetic justice" quality

00:19:00.033 --> 00:19:01.158
to the whole thing.

00:19:01.241 --> 00:19:02.783
You tried to trick
the legal system

00:19:02.866 --> 00:19:05.116
by pretending to be
something you're not,

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:08.450
only to reveal how much
of a criminal you are!

00:19:09.533 --> 00:19:14.158
[screams]

00:19:17.366 --> 00:19:20.241
Today the defendant was given
a second chance at justice

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:21.783
and the truth has prevailed.

00:19:21.866 --> 00:19:25.200
This court has found
Maggey Byrde...

00:19:25.283 --> 00:19:26.241
Not guilty!

00:19:26.325 --> 00:19:30.241
[CROWD cheering, applause]

00:19:30.325 --> 00:19:32.075
[chuckles]

00:19:33.825 --> 00:19:35.366
[MAYA chuckles]

00:19:39.908 --> 00:19:41.200
[TIGRE]
Huh?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.783
Violetta. Why'd you sell
me down da river?

00:19:54.908 --> 00:19:59.700
It's simple. I did it
because I'm a Cadaverini.

00:19:59.783 --> 00:20:03.491
We always get our payback.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:17.283
You know I could never
get angry at you, Violetta.

00:20:17.366 --> 00:20:20.575
I'm so happy now, Don Tigre.

00:20:20.658 --> 00:20:22.866
I'd do anythin' for
youse, dollface.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.200
[growls]

00:20:24.283 --> 00:20:27.783
Damn it all! This is that
gloomy bitch's fault!

00:20:27.866 --> 00:20:31.450
I'm headin' out,
baby! See ya later.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:35.866
[VIOLA]
Don Tigre.

00:20:43.158 --> 00:20:45.033
Thank you so much,
Mister Wright!

00:20:45.116 --> 00:20:48.366
I can hardly believe that you
saved my bacon a second time!

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:50.283
Speaking of food,
we brought some snacks

00:20:50.366 --> 00:20:52.033
to help celebrate
your victory today!

00:20:52.116 --> 00:20:53.241
[MAGGEY gasps]

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:56.825
You know, weenies
aren't really my thing.

00:20:56.908 --> 00:20:58.991
If you wanna thank someone
for getting you out of jail,

00:20:59.075 --> 00:21:01.200
you should thank Gumshoe.

00:21:01.283 --> 00:21:02.866
He worked his tail off.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:06.158
Put in a lot of hours because
he was so worried about you.

00:21:06.241 --> 00:21:07.491
Right up until the last moment

00:21:07.575 --> 00:21:09.283
when he brought in the
final piece of evidence

00:21:09.366 --> 00:21:11.075
to seal the case.

00:21:14.908 --> 00:21:17.533
Are you sure you're not hungry?

00:21:17.616 --> 00:21:18.533
[MAYA gasps]

00:21:18.616 --> 00:21:20.783
How 'bout we go in
halfises, Maya?

00:21:20.866 --> 00:21:22.283
Okay!

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:26.325
Honestly, I was just
being bratty before.

00:21:26.408 --> 00:21:27.908
Weenies are my favorite food!

00:21:27.991 --> 00:21:29.533
[GUMSHOE gasps]

00:21:29.616 --> 00:21:30.408
[PHOENIX chuckles]

00:21:30.491 --> 00:21:31.991
[GUMSHOE]
This is great!

00:21:32.075 --> 00:21:33.533
I am so darn happy!

00:21:33.616 --> 00:21:36.658
You really redeemed
yourself, Dicky!

00:21:36.741 --> 00:21:38.908
[PHOENIX] I think we've all
had our fill of fakes.

00:21:38.991 --> 00:21:41.116
The truth is much
more satisfying.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:44.533
Maggey's reputation and her
plate have both been cleaned.

00:21:44.616 --> 00:21:48.616
And she's ready to enjoy the
next course life has to offer.

00:23:20.616 --> 00:23:22.075
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.158 --> 00:23:24.700
<i>The Silver Star</i> luxuriously
shoots through the night

00:23:24.783 --> 00:23:26.325
along the coastline.

00:23:26.408 --> 00:23:29.450
Maya and I were invited to take
a ride in the ultimate comfort.

00:23:29.533 --> 00:23:31.783
And it turns out Detective
Gumshoe and the judge

00:23:31.866 --> 00:23:33.158
have also come along.

00:23:33.241 --> 00:23:35.158
Unfortunately, the trip
goes off the rails

00:23:35.241 --> 00:23:37.033
when the train is hijacked.

00:23:37.116 --> 00:23:39.325
The perpetrator demands
an impromptu trial

00:23:39.408 --> 00:23:41.575
aboard the non-stop express!

00:23:41.658 --> 00:23:44.116
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:47.741
Next episode: "Northward,
Turnabout Express -- 1st Trial"!

00:23:47.825 --> 00:23:49.033
Take that!
